6120530 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344618 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186120530 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186120530 1071 "The vectors $a_{1}$, $a_{2}$, $a_{3}$, and $a_{4}$ are given below. Determine whether $B = {a_{1}, a_{2}, a_{3}}$ is a basis of $Span{a_{1}, a_{2}, a_{3}, a_{4}}$. If that is the case, find $x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}$, where $a_{4} = x_{1}a_{1} + x_{2}a_{2} + x_{3}a_{3}$.\n$a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}, a_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}, a_{3} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}, a_{4} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186120530 1071 "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ ${a}_{3},$ and ${a}_{4}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3},$ where ${a}_{4}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{4}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186120530 1074 "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+{x}_{3}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=-8,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=7,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n(-8)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+0\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+7\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-8+0+7=-1.$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186120533 1068 #edb/ref 17592186119282 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186120533 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344892 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186120533 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186120533 1071 "![](images/b6/b614e2c3e6abf0d7ddb8399aa7ea78b7a0e618a965ee7b5481edf08310a45031.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $g(t) = ⟨t^{3} - 3t, 3t^{2}⟩$ from $t = 1$ to $t = 2$?" 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186120533 1071 "![](images/b6/b614e2c3e6abf0d7ddb8399aa7ea78b7a0e618a965ee7b5481edf08310a45031.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨{t}^{3}-3t,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩$ from $t=1$ to $t=2?$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186120533 1074 "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-3,\\,6t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2}-3)^{2}+(6t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}-18{t}^{2}+9+36{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+18{t}^{2}+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2}+3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{t}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({t}^{3}+3t){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(8+6)-(1+3) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186120534 1068 #edb/ref 17592186119288 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186120534 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344729 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186120534 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186120534 1071 "![](images/9b/9b83db0bb11b8e4bbcc4b04b7bf696879d4d7f4732d6aef7d005f9da2b625526.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $g(t) = ⟨2t^{3/2}, 3t⟩$ from $t = 0$ to $t = 3$." 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186120534 1071 "![](images/9b/9b83db0bb11b8e4bbcc4b04b7bf696879d4d7f4732d6aef7d005f9da2b625526.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨2{t}^{3/2},\\,3t⟩$ from $t=0$ to $t=3.$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186120534 1074 "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\sqrt{t},\\,3⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3\\sqrt{t})^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9t+9} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3\\sqrt{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3(t+1)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2(t+1)^{3/2}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =16-2 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124458 1038 #edb/ref 17592186344998 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124458 1038 #edb/ref 17592186344999 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124459 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345000 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124459 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345006 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124463 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345010 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124463 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345011 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124518 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345001 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124519 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345003 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124519 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345004 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124519 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345005 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124520 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345002 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124564 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345007 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124564 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345008 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124564 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345009 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186124568 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345320 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186125225 1068 #edb/ref 17592186123920 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186125225 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344731 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186125225 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186125225 1071 "Let $U$ be the set of polynomials of the form $ax^{3}$, where $a ∈ R$. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The zero-polynomial belongs to $U$.\n2. For any $p(x), q(x) ∈ U$, we have $p(x) + q(x) = q(x) + p(x)$.\n3. For any $p(x), q(x), r(x) ∈ U$, we have $[p(x) - q(x)] - r(x) = p(x) - [q(x) - r(x)]$." 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186125225 1071 "Let $U$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{3},$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The zero-polynomial belongs to $U.$\n- For any $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x).$\n- For any $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in U,$ we have $[p(x)-q(x)]-r(x)=p(x)-[q(x)-r(x)].$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186125225 1074 "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the zero-polynomial can be represented as \n\n$$\n0=0\\cdot {x}^{3}.\n$$\n\n \nHence, $0\\in U.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\np(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x)\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is commutative.\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, consider polynomials $p(x)={x}^{3},$ $q(x)=2{x}^{3},$ and $r(x)=3{x}^{3}$ from $U.$ Then: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[p(x)-q(x)]-r(x) & =[{x}^{3}-2{x}^{3}]-3{x}^{3} \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-3{x}^{3} \\\\  & =-4{x}^{3} \\\\ p(x)-[q(x)-r(x)] & ={x}^{3}-[2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{3}] \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-[-{x}^{3}] \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $[p(x)-q(x)]-r(x)\\ne p(x)-[q(x)-r(x)].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186129099 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345178 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186129099 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345179 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186129100 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345180 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186129101 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345181 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186129101 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345182 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186129101 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345183 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186129138 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345195 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186129138 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345196 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186129138 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345197 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186129138 1038