rue] [17592186133836 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345225 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186133836 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345226 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186134517 1068 #edb/ref 17592186133110 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186134517 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344698 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186134517 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186134517 1071 "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x, y) = \\frac{12x}{y - 1}$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t) = t^{2}i + (t + 1)j$ for $t ∈ [\\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{6}]$." 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186134517 1071 "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{12x}{y-1}$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(t+1)\\,j\\,$ for $t\\in [\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{6}].$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186134517 1074 "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(t+1)\\,j$, then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2}$ and $y=t+1.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{12x}{y-1}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{12{t}^{2}}{(t+1)-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12{t}^{2}}{t} \\\\  & =12t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{6}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{6}}12t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=4{t}^{2}+1,$ $\\text{d}u=8t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{6}}12t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{9}^{25}\\frac{3}{2}{u}^{1/2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={u}^{3/2}{|}_{9}^{25} \\\\  & ={25}^{3/2}-{9}^{3/2} \\\\  & =125-27 \\\\  & =98\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152122 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345221 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152123 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345227 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152125 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345206 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152125 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345228 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152154 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345029 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152154 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345057 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152154 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345059 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152154 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345061 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152154 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345062 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152155 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345063 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152155 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345064 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152156 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345030 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152156 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345044 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152156 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345046 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152156 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345047 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152157 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345058 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152159 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345072 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152159 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345073 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152159 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345074 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186152159 1038 #edb/r