#edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180277 1071 "Let $R = [15, 20] \\cdot [3, 5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = x - 3y$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$U(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$\n\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$,\nwhat is the missing expression in the double summation above?" 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186180277 1071 "Let $R=[15,20]\\times [3,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x-3y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$\nwhat is the missing expression in the double summation above?" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180277 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=x-3y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x-3y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/de/de36b521dea1f925754a9c630c3d4a2c405c087a191138f1eaaa5771becb8c21.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}.$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180278 1068 #edb/ref 17592186179182 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186180278 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344517 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180278 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180278 1071 "Let $R = [- 3, 2] \\cdot [4, 7]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = y - 3x + 2$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$U(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$\n\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186180278 1071 "Let $R=[-3,2]\\times [4,7]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=y-3x+2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180278 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=y-3x+2$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=y-3x+2$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ff/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/74/74d546d91e145efea49b70af56cb472e8bbbd1417725cd7fa92a3a278cad75ea.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})={y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}+2)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}+2.$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180280 1068 #edb/ref 17592186179194 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186180280 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344838 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180280 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180280 1071 "Let $R = [2, 4] \\cdot [2, 4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = 2x + y + 1$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$U(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186180280 1071 "Let $R=[2,4]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=2x+y+1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180280 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y+1$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y+1$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/6e/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=2{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}+1)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $2{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}+1.$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180285 1068 #edb/ref 17592186179224 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186180285 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344710 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180285 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180285 1071 "![](images/10/103c586778cdd8181fdc8396a92472df0525fc8e1c77fde9a7c3f731dca6df07.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_(C)F \\cdot dr$, where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $OABO$, shown in the diagram above, traversed in the counterclockwise direction?" 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186180285 1071 "![](images/10/103c586778cdd8181fdc8396a92472df0525fc8e1c77fde9a7c3f731dca6df07.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $OABO,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the counterclockwise direction?" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180285 1074 "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed in counterclockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={C}_{1}\\cup {-{C}_{2}}\\cup {C}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{2}$ is the same path as ${C}_{2}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180286 1068 #edb/ref 17592186179230 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186180286 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344918 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180286 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180286 1071 "![](images/9f/9fd222d255fd1a37f00cbe7c9abf6af0d0e3af92f9ac581591bb1062780e69fa.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_(C)F \\cdot dr$, where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $ABCA$, shown in the diagram above, traversed in the **clockwise** direction?" 13194139533428 17592186045585 false] [17592186180286 1071 "![](images/9f/9fd222d255fd1a37f00cbe7c9abf6af0d0e3af92f9ac581591bb1062780e69fa.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $ABCA,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the **clockwise** direction?" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186180286 1074 "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed clockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={-{C}_{1}}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {-{C}_{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{1}$ and $-{C}_{3}$ are the same paths as ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{3}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186184173 1038 #edb/ref 17592186344974 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186184234 1038 #edb/ref 17592186344961 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186184338 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345162 13194139533428 17592186045585 true] [17592186184339 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345161 13194139533428 175921860